     "label": "Loose tiles in the wall",
     "reveal": {
      "title": "Diary, wrapped in oilcloth",
      "clue": "diary_1948",
      "text": "Transit Authority, Ellery St. Maintenance\nMarch 1948\nThey're closing the station. Officially, water in the tunnels. The men say it's the voices from the old token hall after the last train.\nKessler from upstairs paid me to keep a box down here, out of the way, 'for family reasons.' Heavy. Something shifts inside when nobody's touching it.\nApril. The box is gone. Kessler's boy came for it, with a lady I didn't like the look of. I'm putting in for a transfer."
     }
    }
